<node id="idea:A1-11">
  <data key="d0">idea</data>
  <data key="d1">Constraint-aware factor-graph estimation of mobile device compromise for banking apps</data>
  <data key="d2">A1</data>
  <data key="d3">2026-09-30</data>
  <data key="d4">fraud</data>
  <data key="d5">Malicious apps (fake hospital-appointment apps, adult-content lures) empty accounts by abusing accessibility services, overlays and SMS access. Banking SDK signals are sparse, noisy and often missing, so rule engines misfire both ways.</data>
  <data key="d6">The banking SDK observes a sparse set of signals: accessibility-service enablement and event rates, overlay-window presence, notification-listener or SMS-read capability, screen-share state, input-event timing, installed-package risk and OS patch level. A factor graph links hidden compromise-state variables (overlay attack, SMS interception, remote control, benign) to these observations. Hard factors encode OS permission logic, for example that SMS interception is impossible without READ_SMS or notification access, and overlays require SYSTEM_ALERT_WINDOW. Soft factors are learned likelihoods. Neural message passing with hard-constraint projection gives calibrated posteriors even when most observations are missing. These posteriors gate specific flows: SMS-OTP flows are disabled when P(SMS interception) is high, and payee addition when P(remote control) is high.</data>
  <data key="d7">0.2315</data>
</node>
