<node id="idea:A1-21">
  <data key="d0">idea</data>
  <data key="d1">Crowd-relayed settlement of offline payments via delay-tolerant store-carry-forward routing</data>
  <data key="d2">A1</data>
  <data key="d3">2026-09-30</data>
  <data key="d4">payments</data>
  <data key="d5">Offline digital payments (offline CBDC, UPI Lite-style wallets) carry double-spend risk that grows with the time until settlement. Remote regions (e.g. RBI's push for credit and payments in J&amp;K) can stay offline for days.</data>
  <data key="d6">Each offline payment is packaged as an encrypted, signed bundle. Opted-in nearby devices act as carriers and store and forward bundles over BLE or Wi-Fi Direct. Routing is on-demand: a bundle goes to the carriers predicted, from their mobility history, to reach connectivity soonest, rather than flooding to everyone. The first carrier to reach the network submits the bundle. The ledger deduplicates by bundle ID and returns a signed receipt, which pays the carrier a micro-incentive and propagates back as a settlement acknowledgement. The payee's offline wallet can raise its offline limit when earlier bundles are acknowledged.</data>
  <data key="d7">0.1783</data>
</node>
