<node id="idea:A2b-14">
  <data key="d0">idea</data>
  <data key="d1">Purchase-session binding for UPI: aggregating split payments per merchant session for correct MDR and fewer false fraud flags</data>
  <data key="d2">A2b</data>
  <data key="d3">2026-09-30</data>
  <data key="d4">payments</data>
  <data key="d5">RBI backs MDR on UPI payments above ₹2,000, which gives merchants and payers an incentive to split payments. Banks already flag repeated ₹2,000 payments as suspicious, which hurts legitimate split payments.</data>
  <data key="d6">A merchant QR or intent carries a session identifier signed by the merchant's PSP, derived from the cart/bill. Payments carrying the same session ID within a window are aggregated at the acquirer for MDR computation, removing the split-to-evade incentive. On the risk side, the payer's PSP treats payments sharing a verified session ID as one purchase, so legitimate splits (limits, multiple sources) are not flagged. Splits without a session ID, to the same payee in a short window, keep full scrutiny.</data>
  <data key="d7">0.2613</data>
</node>
